# CR 702.145b: daybound means "if it is night and this permanent is represented by a double-faced card, it enters
# transformed" - the permanent's daybound, whatever gives it (the example under CR 712.13a: a double-faced card entering
# as a copy of a daybound creature at night enters with its back face up). Glasspool Mimic, a modal double-faced card
# (CR 712.3: one may transform), enters at night as a copy of a Clone that copied Outland Liberator: the Mimic has daybound
# as it would enter, so it enters transformed - back face up, still a copy of Outland Liberator (CR 707.2), and never
# transformed after (CR 712.14a: entering transformed is no transformation). The Clone, no double-faced card, stays front
# face up at night (CR 701.27c); the Liberator itself became Frenzied Trapbreaker as night came.
#
# Turn 1: Forest and Mox Emerald cast Outland Liberator (it becomes day, CR 702.145d); Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire cast
# Clone, copying it. Bot2 casts nothing on turn 2, so turn 3 is night (CR 731.2). Turn 3: Forest, Emerald and Sapphire
# cast Glasspool Mimic, copying the Clone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Outland Liberator
Clone
Island
Glasspool Mimic
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

